; A cost total stated against no units.
;
; `{{50.00 CAD}}` is the doubled-brace spelling of `@@ 50.00 CAD` — both say
; the figure is the total rather than a rate per unit. Against `0` units
; there is no rate to derive and nothing to spread the figure over, so the
; refusal `@@` gets belongs here too: read as unpriced, the total is dropped,
; the split valued at zero, and GnuCash scrubs the whole 50.00 into an
; Imbalance while the run reports success.
;
; `{50.00 CAD}` — the single brace, per unit — is not this: it weighs
; units × cost = 0, which is the truth about a posting holding nothing.
;
; What this fixture produces: a refusal saying there is nowhere to attach the
; total.
;
; Verified by tests/integration/test_beancount_reads_what_a_person_writes.py.
